{"id":"int-18656dc8","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-23T19:30:07.369623Z","actor":"John","issue_id":"tcg-card-sniper-dev-nf4","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Fixed by 6e5866d. Root cause: Railway sets NODE_ENV=production on the server service, so pnpm install skipped devDependencies. Build then failed first on prisma (fixed 8e034cd), then tsc (fixed 8a51aef), then @types/node. Final fix: in railway.json buildCommand, prefix install with NODE_ENV=development and use --force so devDeps are reinstalled over the Nixpacks step-7 prod-only install. Deploy succeeded, server running on port 8080."}}
{"id":"int-94fbd153","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-23T19:52:29.507035Z","actor":"John","issue_id":"tcg-card-sniper-dev-tdj","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Fixed client deploy. Root cause: client service was reading the SHARED root /railway.json which contains the server's build/start commands, regardless of railwayConfigFile or rootDirectory overrides on the service. railway up from repo root always includes / railway.json in the build context. Working fix: (1) set buildCommand='npm install --include=dev && npm run build' and startCommand='npx serve -s dist -l $PORT --no-clipboard' directly on the client service via GraphQL serviceInstanceUpdate, (2) deploy with 'railway up ./client --path-as-root --service client' so only the client/ subdir becomes the build context (no stray /railway.json). HTTP 200 confirmed at poke-sniper.up.railway.app."}}
{"id":"int-8df395d1","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-23T20:54:45.299618Z","actor":"John","issue_id":"tcg-card-sniper-dev-dgc","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Lifted reValueWithAnnotation + bestSingleMarket from routes/lots.ts to services/lotValuation.ts. Changed auto-value computation to walk Lot.parsedCards JSON, summing min/max market × quantity per parsed card, but skipping any entry whose name (case-insensitive trim) matches the Card.name of a user-added card. Prevents double-counting when user picks the correct printing of a card the AI already auto-resolved. 194/194 server tests still passing. Commit e19421a."}}
